# LaTeX build artifacts and scratch renders (regenerate with: python build.py)
build/
*.aux
*.log
*.out
*.toc
*.fls
*.fdb_latexmk
*.synctex.gz

# No assembled volume and no PDF is ever published. Only the Markdown chapters
# and the projects are, which is what mdbuild.py writes. These are blanket rules
# rather than named files, so a new output name cannot slip through: the whole
# volume, a single unit of it, or anything else.
*.pdf
*.html

# Named explicitly as well, so the intent survives anyone relaxing the rules
# above.
robot-joint-node.pdf
robot-joint-node.html

# Per-chapter deliverables, built on demand with: python build.py --chapter N
chapter-*.pdf
chapter-*.html

# Local virtual environments and editor state
.venv/
venv/
.vscode/
.idea/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Journals and correspondence never reach a published repository, private
# shares included. They live in the catalogue, which is local only. A published
# repository carries the work, never the running record of doing it. This is a
# guard rather than a reminder: the rule has held by discipline so far, and a
# rule that lives only in someone's head is one copy away from being broken.
private_journal/
correspondence/
DIARY*.md
